"""gen_cli_menu.py -- flat MenuBuilder generator for the IronKernel 64 core 0 CLI.

Implements Z:\\AI-LinuxScripts\\agent-markdowns\\embedded\\MenuBuilder.md (flat
FUNCTION:COMMAND:DESCRIPTION format) as a deterministic script. It is NOT a copy of
RTLNet's gen_menu.py: that tool implements the hierarchical (modes) variant
(MenuBuilder_hierarchical.md) and its 1225-line menu.c does not fit the 256 KiB LMB.
Input : fw_c64/cli/cli_commands.txt
Output: fw_c64/cli/menu.h, menu.c, menu_commands.def, MenuDocumentation.md and the desktop
        harness fw_c64/cli/desktop/{menu_callback_Test.c, main.c, Makefile, build.bat}.
Revision rows come from lines "# REVISION: MM-DD-YYYY | text" in the .txt (append-only).
Every output is a pure function of the .txt, so --check regenerates in memory and
compares byte for byte (the check_menu step).
Usage: python gen_cli_menu.py [--check]   Exit 0 written/identical, 1 input error or difference.
"""
